              "# GhostShellAgent – Fortgeschrittene Architektur & Implementierung\n\nDieses Dokument fasst alle vorgeschlagenen Erweiterungen für den **GhostShellAgent** zusammen und liefert konkrete Code‑ und Konfigurations‑Snippets.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Clustering & Load-Balancing\n\n### 1.1 Node.js Cluster-API (PM2)\n\n```js\n// cluster.js\nimport cluster from 'cluster';\nimport os from 'os';\nimport { startServer } from './ghostShellAgent';\n\nif (cluster.isPrimary) {\n  const cpus = os.cpus().length;\n  for (let i = 0; i < cpus; i++) {\n    cluster.fork();\n  }\n  cluster.on('exit', (worker) => {\n    console.log(`Worker ${worker.process.pid} crashed, forking new one`);\n    cluster.fork();\n  });\n} else {\n  startServer(); // aus ghostShellAgent exportiert\n}\n```\n\n### 1.2 NGINX Reverse Proxy\n\n```nginx\n# /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/ghostshell\nupstream ghostshell {\n    server 127.0.0.1:3000;\n    server 127.0.0.1:3001;\n    # ... entsprechend Cluster-Ports\n}\nserver {\n    listen 80;\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass http://ghostshell;\n        proxy_http_version 1.1;\n        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header Connection \"upgrade\";\n        proxy_set_header Host $host;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Auth & Ratelimits\n\n### 2.1 JWT-Middleware für Socket.io\n\n```ts\n// auth.ts\nimport jwt from 'jsonwebtoken';\nimport { Socket } from 'socket.io';\n\nexport function socketAuth(secret: string) {\n  return (socket: Socket, next: (err?: Error) => void) => {\n    const token = socket.handshake.auth.token;\n    try {\n      const payload = jwt.verify(token, secret);\n      (socket as any).user = payload;\n      next();\n    } catch (err) {\n      next(new Error('Authentication error'));\n    }\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### 2.2 Ratelimit mit socket.io-rate-limiter\n\n```js\nimport { RateLimiterMemory } from 'rate-limiter-flexible';\n\nconst limiter = new RateLimiterMemory({ points: 10, duration: 60 });\n\nioc.use(async (socket, next) => {\n  try {\n    await limiter.consume(socket.handshake.address);\n    next();\n  } catch {\n    next(new Error('Too many requests'));\n  }\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Observability & Monitoring\n\n### 3.1 Prometheus-Metrics (Node)\n\n```ts\nimport { Counter, Gauge, collectDefaultMetrics, register } from 'prom-client';\ncollectDefaultMetrics();\nconst connCounter = new Counter({ name: 'ghost_connections_total', help: 'Total WS connections' });\nconst latencyGauge = new Gauge({ name: 'ghost_response_latency', help: 'Response latency ms' });\n\napp.get('/metrics', async (_, res) => {\n  res.set('Content-Type', register.contentType);\n  res.end(await register.metrics());\n});\n\nioc.on('connection', socket => {\n  connCounter.inc();\n  socket.on('user_message', async (msg, cb) => {\n    const start = Date.now();\n    const result = await handleMessage(msg);\n    latencyGauge.set(Date.now() - start);\n    cb(result);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### 3.2 Structured Logging mit Pino\n\n```ts\nimport pino from 'pino';\nexport const logger = pino({ level: 'info', transport: { target: 'pino-pretty' } });\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Advanced Scheduling\n\n### 4.1 Event-Driven mit chokidar\n\n```js\nimport chokidar from 'chokidar';\nimport { runSelfLearn } from './autoCommitAgent';\n\nchokidar.watch('newadvancedconversations/*.json').on('add', () => {\n  runSelfLearn();\n});\n```\n\n### 4.2 Adaptive Intervalle\n\n```js\nlet intervalMs = 6 * 3600 * 1000;\nfunction scheduleAdaptive() {\n  setTimeout(async () => {\n    const newCount = await countNewFragments();\n    intervalMs = newCount > 10 ? 2*3600*1000 : 12*3600*1000;\n    runSelfLearn();\n    scheduleAdaptive();\n  }, intervalMs);\n}\nscheduleAdaptive();\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sigil-Alerts & UI-Integration\n\n### 5.1 WebSocket-Event im Agent\n\n```ts\nif (result.energy > threshold) {\n  socket.emit('sigil_alert', {\n    id: 'aeon:2025-0626-HIGH-ENERGY',\n    effect: 'pulse-red'\n  });\n}\n```\n\n### 5.2 Client-Side Darstellung\n\n```js\nsocket.on('sigil_alert', sigil => {\n  const el = document.createElement('div');\n  el.className = `sigil ${sigil.effect}`;\n  el.textContent = sigil.id;\n  document.body.appendChild(el);\n  setTimeout(() => el.remove(), 5000);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Stateful Dialog-Manager & Multi-User\n\n### 6.1 Simple In-Memory Session Store\n\n```ts\nconst sessions = new Map<string, { history: any[] }>();\nioc.on('connection', socket => {\n  sessions.set(socket.id, { history: [] });\n  socket.on('user_message', msg => {\n    const session = sessions.get(socket.id);\n    session.history.push(msg);\n    const response = ghost.harmonize(...);\n    socket.emit('ghost_response', response);\n  });\n  socket.on('disconnect', () => {\n    sessions.delete(socket.id);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### 6.2 Gemeinsamer Raum (Ritualraum)\n\n```ts\nconst rooms = new Map<string, Set<string>>();\nioc.on('connection', socket => {\n  socket.on('join_room', roomId => {\n    socket.join(roomId);\n    if (!rooms.has(roomId)) rooms.set(roomId, new Set());\n    rooms.get(roomId).add(socket.id);\n  });\n\n  socket.on('room_message', ({ roomId, msg }) => {\n    ghost.train(...);\n    const res = ghost.harmonize(...);\n    ioc.to(roomId).emit('room_response', res);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n✨ Mit diesen Implementierungen wird dein GhostShellAgent zu einem **skalierbaren**, **sicheren**, **observierbaren** und **mandalischen** System. Jeder Abschnitt kann modular aktiviert werden. Viel Spaß beim Hardcoden und fraktalen Erschaffen! 🌌🚀"
