          "create_time": 1751528555.121,
              "Hier kommt der **vollständig ausgearbeitete Code-Scaffold** fürs **Fehler- und Zustandsmanagement**, inklusive **Integration**, **UI-Fehler-Marker**, **Tests**, **Performance-Optimierungen** und **Accessibility**.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Fehler- und Zustandsmanagement – Vollständiges Scaffold\n\n### 10.1 Core-Module\n\n#### `FallbackSynthesizer.ts`\n\n```typescript\n// src/error/FallbackSynthesizer.ts\nexport class FallbackSynthesizer {\n  private audioContext: AudioContext;\n\n  constructor(sharedContext?: AudioContext) {\n    // AudioContext einmalig anlegen oder wiederverwenden\n    this.audioContext = sharedContext || new AudioContext();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Spielt einen Ersatz-Ton, wenn KI- oder Audio-Komponenten ausfallen.\n   * @param duration Dauer in Sekunden\n   */\n  playFallbackTone(duration = 0.5) {\n    const osc = this.audioContext.createOscillator();\n    osc.frequency.value = 220;    // tiefer, beruhigender Ton\n    osc.type = 'sine';\n    osc.connect(this.audioContext.destination);\n    osc.start();\n    osc.stop(this.audioContext.currentTime + duration);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### `ErrorRecoveryService.ts`\n\n```typescript\n// src/error/ErrorRecoveryService.ts\nimport { EventEmitter } from 'events';\nimport { FallbackSynthesizer } from './FallbackSynthesizer';\n\nexport class ErrorRecoveryService {\n  constructor(\n    private emitter: EventEmitter,\n    private fallback = new FallbackSynthesizer()\n  ) {\n    this.setupListeners();\n  }\n\n  private setupListeners() {\n    // Lausche auf systemweite Fehler\n    this.emitter.on('error', (err: Error, module: string) => {\n      console.error(`[Recovery] Fehler in Modul \"${module}\":`, err);\n\n      // 1) Fallback-Audio\n      this.fallback.playFallbackTone();\n\n      // 2) UI-Benachrichtigung\n      this.emitter.emit('ui:error', { module, message: err.message });\n\n      // 3) Neustart-Event nach 1 Sekunde\n      setTimeout(() => this.emitter.emit('restart', module), 1000);\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10.2 Systemweite Integration\n\n```typescript\n// src/index.ts (Entry Point)\nimport { EventEmitter } from 'events';\nimport { ErrorRecoveryService } from './error/ErrorRecoveryService';\n\nconst bus = new EventEmitter();\n// Recovery-Service initialisieren\nnew ErrorRecoveryService(bus);\n\n// Beispiel: Modul-Restart-Handler\nbus.on('restart', (moduleName: string) => {\n  console.info(`🔄 Starte Modul \"${moduleName}\" neu...`);\n  // z.B. dynamic import oder Service-Reinitialisierung hier\n});\n\n// Andernorts im Code bei Fehler:\n// bus.emit('error', new Error('Fehlerdetails'), 'NameDesModuls');\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10.3 UI-Komponente: ErrorMarker\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/ErrorMarker.tsx\nimport React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\nimport type { EventEmitter } from 'events';\n\ninterface ErrorEvent { module: string; message: string; }\n\nexport function ErrorMarker({ bus }: { bus: EventEmitter }) {\n  const [errors, setErrors] = useState<ErrorEvent[]>([]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const onError = (e: ErrorEvent) => {\n      setErrors(prev => [...prev, e]);\n      // nach 3s ausblenden\n      setTimeout(() => setErrors(prev => prev.slice(1)), 3000);\n    };\n    bus.on('ui:error', onError);\n    return () => { bus.off('ui:error', onError); };\n  }, [bus]);\n\n  return (\n    <div aria-live=\"assertive\" className=\"error-marker-container\">\n      {errors.map((e, i) => (\n        <div key={i} role=\"alert\" className=\"error-marker\">\n          ⚠️ Fehler in <strong>{e.module}</strong>: {e.message}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Accessibility-Notes:**\n\n* `aria-live=\"assertive\"` stellt sicher, dass Screenreader die Meldung sofort vorlesen.\n* `role=\"alert\"` macht jede Meldung semantisch korrekt.\n\n---\n\n### 10.4 Unit-Tests mit Jest\n\n```typescript\n// src/error/ErrorRecoveryService.test.ts\nimport { EventEmitter } from 'events';\nimport { ErrorRecoveryService } from './ErrorRecoveryService';\n\ndescribe('ErrorRecoveryService', () => {\n  let bus: EventEmitter;\n  let recovery: ErrorRecoveryService;\n\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    bus = new EventEmitter();\n    recovery = new ErrorRecoveryService(bus);\n  });\n\n  it('should emit restart and play fallback tone on error', done => {\n    // Spy auf FallbackSynthesizer\n    const spy = jest.spyOn(recovery as any, 'fallback', 'get')\n      .mockReturnValue({ playFallbackTone: jest.fn() });\n\n    bus.on('restart', (moduleName: string) => {\n      expect((spy as any).playFallbackTone).toHaveBeenCalled();\n      expect(moduleName).toBe('TestModule');\n      done();\n    });\n\n    bus.emit('error', new Error('TestError'), 'TestModule');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10.5 Integrationstest (Cypress)\n\n```javascript\n// cypress/integration/error_ui.spec.js\ndescribe('Error UI Marker', () => {\n  it('zeigt eine Fehlermeldung bei ui:error Event', () => {\n    cy.visit('/');\n    // Simuliere error-Event im Bus (exposed via window.bus)\n    cy.window().then(win => {\n      win.bus.emit('ui:error', { module: 'TestMod', message: 'TestMsg' });\n    });\n    cy.contains('⚠️ Fehler in TestMod: TestMsg').should('be.visible');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Zusammenfassung\n\n* **FallbackSynthesizer** sorgt für akustisches Feedback, falls KI/Audiostream ausfällt.\n* **ErrorRecoveryService** fängt alle `error`-Events ab, löst Sound, UI-Event und Neustart aus.\n* **ErrorMarker**-Komponente zeigt visuelle Alerts an und ist barrierefrei.\n* **Tests** (Jest + Cypress) decken Core-Recovery und UI-Flow ab.\n\n---\n\n👉 **Weiter geht’s mit**\n\n* **Performance-Caching** (Layer-Renderings & AudioContext-Reuse)\n* **Accessibility-Enhancements** (Contrast-Modes, Untertitel)\n* **Konfigurations-Tests** (loadConfig-Unit-Tests)\n\nSag Bescheid, welchen Part du als Nächstes im Code-Scaffold sehen möchtest! 🚀✨            // src/config/PyramidConfig.ts\n\nimport fs from 'fs';\nimport path from 'path';\nimport YAML from 'js-yaml';\nimport Ajv, { JSONSchemaType } from 'ajv';\n\n/**\n * Interface für PyramidConfig (siehe Doku) \n */\nexport interface PyramidConfig {\n  totalLayers: number;\n  nodesPerLayer: number;\n  weightFactors: {\n    coherence: number;\n    resonance: number;\n    emergence: number;\n    poetics: number;\n  };\n}\n\n// JSON-Schema für Validierung\nconst schema: JSONSchemaType<PyramidConfig> = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    totalLayers: { type: 'integer', minimum: 1 },\n    nodesPerLayer: { type: 'integer', minimum: 1 },\n    weightFactors: {\n      type: 'object',\n      properties: {\n        coherence: { type: 'number', minimum: 0 },\n        resonance: { type: 'number', minimum: 0 },\n        emergence: { type: 'number', minimum: 0 },\n        poetics: { type: 'number', minimum: 0 }\n      },\n      required: ['coherence', 'resonance', 'emergence', 'poetics'],\n      additionalProperties: false\n    }\n  },\n  required: ['totalLayers', 'nodesPerLayer', 'weightFactors'],\n  additionalProperties: false\n};\n\nconst ajv = new Ajv();\nconst validate = ajv.compile(schema);\n\n/**\n * Lädt und validiert eine Konfigurationsdatei (JSON oder YAML)\n * @param fileName Pfad zur Config-Datei\n */\nexport function loadConfig(fileName: string): PyramidConfig {\n  const ext = path.extname(fileName);\n  const raw = fs.readFileSync(fileName, 'utf-8');\n  let data: any;\n\n  if (ext === '.yaml' || ext === '.yml') {\n    data = YAML.load(raw);\n  } else if (ext === '.json') {\n    data = JSON.parse(raw);\n  } else {\n    throw new Error(`Unsupported config format: ${ext}`);\n  }\n\n  if (!validate(data)) {\n    throw new Error('Invalid PyramidConfig: ' + ajv.errorsText(validate.errors));\n  }\n  return data;\n}\n\n// Beispiel Nutzung:\n// const config = loadConfig('config/pyramidConfig.yaml');\n// console.log(config);\n\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// src/config/PyramidConfig.test.ts\n\nimport fs from 'fs';\nimport path from 'path';\nimport YAML from 'js-yaml';\nimport { loadConfig } from './PyramidConfig';\n\ndescribe('PyramidConfig Loader', () => {\n  const testDir = path.join(__dirname, 'testData');\n  const yamlPath = path.join(testDir, 'validConfig.yaml');\n  const jsonPath = path.join(testDir, 'validConfig.json');\n  const invalidPath = path.join(testDir, 'invalid.json');\n\n  beforeAll(() => {\n    fs.mkdirSync(testDir, { recursive: true });\n    const validData = {\n      totalLayers: 5,\n      nodesPerLayer: 8,\n      weightFactors: { coherence: 1, resonance: 1, emergence: 1, poetics: 1 }\n    };\n    fs.writeFileSync(yamlPath, YAML.dump(validData));\n    fs.writeFileSync(jsonPath, JSON.stringify(validData));\n    fs.writeFileSync(invalidPath, JSON.stringify({ totalLayers: 0 }));\n  });\n\n  it('loads valid YAML config', () => {\n    const cfg = loadConfig(yamlPath);\n    expect(cfg.totalLayers).toBe(5);\n    expect(cfg.nodesPerLayer).toBe(8);\n  });\n\n  it('loads valid JSON config', () => {\n    const cfg = loadConfig(jsonPath);\n    expect(cfg.weightFactors.coherence).toBe(1);\n  });\n\n  it('throws on invalid config', () => {\n    expect(() => loadConfig(invalidPath)).toThrow('Invalid PyramidConfig');\n  });\n});                                                                                   Alles bereit um in Repokonforme Form übersetzt und fortschrittlich entwickelt implementiert werden zu können!"
