              "# 1. Projekt-Scaffold & Repo‑Struktur\n\nEine pnpm‑Monorepo mit drei Packages (`agent`, `ui`, `common`), CI/CD und TypeScript‑Support.\n\n```\n/ (Root)\n├─ package.json\n├─ pnpm-workspace.yaml\n├─ tsconfig.json\n├─ .github/\n│  └─ workflows/\n│     └─ ci.yml\n├─ packages/\n│  ├─ agent/\n│  │  ├─ package.json\n│  │  ├─ tsconfig.json\n│  │  └─ src/\n│  │     └─ agents/\n│  │        └─ CosmicTheoryAgent.ts\n│  ├─ common/\n│  │  ├─ package.json\n│  │  ├─ tsconfig.json\n│  │  └─ src/\n│  │     ├─ schemas/\n│  │     │  └─ theory-agent-config.json\n│  │     ├─ utils/\n│  │     │  └─ validateConfig.ts\n│  │     └─ layers/\n│  │        ├─ Layer.ts\n│  │        └─ weights.ts\n│  └─ ui/\n│     ├─ package.json\n│     ├─ tsconfig.json\n│     └─ src/\n│        ├─ components/\n│        │  ├─ SigilSelector.tsx\n│        │  ├─ ThreeDPyramid.tsx\n│        │  └─ MetricsDashboard.tsx\n│        ├─ audio/\n│        │  └─ PhiTone.ts\n│        └─ App.tsx\n```\n\n## Root-Konfiguration\n\n**pnpm-workspace.yaml**\n\n```yaml\npackages:\n  - \"packages/*\"\n```\n\n**package.json**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"aeonai\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"pnpm -r run build\",\n    \"lint\": \"pnpm -r run lint\",\n    \"test\": \"pnpm -r run test\",\n    \"clean\": \"pnpm -r run clean\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.0.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"^8.0.0\",\n    \"prettier\": \"^2.0.0\",\n    \"jest\": \"^29.0.0\",\n    \"cypress\": \"^12.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**tsconfig.json** (Root)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"references\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/common\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/agent\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/ui\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## CI/CD (GitHub Actions)\n\nFür automatisierte Validierung, Tests und Build-Prozess nutzen wir folgenden Workflow:\n\n**.github/workflows/ci.yml**\n\n```yaml\nname: CI & Config-Validation\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n    paths:\n      - 'src/config/TheoryAgentConfig.ts'\n      - 'config/**/*.yaml'\n      - 'config/**/*.json'\n      - 'src/**'\n      - '.github/workflows/**'\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n\njobs:\n  setup:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    outputs:\n      node-modules-cache-key: ${{ steps.cache-modules.outputs.cache-hit }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n        with:\n          node-version: 18\n          cache: 'pnpm'\n      - name: Cache pnpm store\n        id: cache-modules\n        uses: actions/cache@v3\n        with:\n          path: ~/.pnpm-store\n          key: pnpm-store-${{ hashFiles('pnpm-lock.yaml') }}\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: pnpm install\n\n  validate-config:\n    needs: setup\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n        with:\n          node-version: 18\n          cache: 'pnpm'\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: pnpm install\n      - name: Validate config files against JSON-Schema\n        run: |\n          npx ajv validate \\\n            -s packages/common/src/schemas/theory-agent-config.json \\\n            -d config/cosmic-theory-agent.yaml \\\n            -c\n\n  test:\n    needs: [setup, validate-config]\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        node: [18]\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n        with:\n          node-version: ${{ matrix.node }}\n          cache: 'pnpm'\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: pnpm install\n      - name: Run ESLint\n        run: pnpm lint\n      - name: Run Unit & Integration Tests\n        run: pnpm test -- --coverage\n      - name: Upload coverage to Codecov\n        uses: codecov/codecov-action@v3\n        with:\n          files: coverage/*.json\n\n  build:\n    needs: test\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n        with:\n          node-version: 18\n          cache: 'pnpm'\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: pnpm install\n      - name: Build\n        run: pnpm build\n      - name: Archive production artifacts\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3\n        with:\n          name: dist\n          path: dist/\n```\n\n**Workflow-Beschreibung**\n\n* **validate-config**: Nutzt AJV und das JSON-Schema in `packages/common/src/schemas/theory-agent-config.json` zur Validierung aller YAML/JSON-Konfigurationsdateien im `config/`-Verzeichnis.\n* **test**: Führt Linting (ESLint) sowie Jest-Unit- und Integrationstests aus und lädt Coverage-Daten zu Codecov hoch.\n* **build**: Erstellt Produktions-Builds und archiviert die Artefakte für Releases.\n* **Caching**: Der pnpm-Store wird zwischengespeichert, um Installationszeiten zu minimieren.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Config‑Schema & AJV‑Integration\n\nUm typsichere und validierte Agentenkonfigurationen sicherzustellen, legen wir ein JSON‑Schema in `packages/common/src/schemas/theory-agent-config.json` an und verwenden AJV zur Laufzeit­validierung.\n\n### 2.1 JSON‑Schema\n\n```jsonc\n// packages/common/src/schemas/theory-agent-config.json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"TheoryAgentConfig\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"version\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"depth\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1 },\n    \"topN\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1 },\n    \"cacheSize\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1 },\n    \"breakerErrorThreshold\": { \"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 100 },\n    \"resetTimeout\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1000 },\n    \"rollingWindowMs\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1 },\n    \"rollingBuckets\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1 },\n    \"regression\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"maxDepth\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1 },\n        \"timeout\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1000 }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"maxDepth\", \"timeout\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"fractalOptions\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"depth\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1 },\n        \"method\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"wavelet\",\"boxCount\",\"fourier\"] }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"depth\",\"method\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"pythonFallback\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"uri\" },\n        \"timeout\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1000 }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"url\",\"timeout\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"sigilAlert\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dataMissing\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"success\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"minPoetics\": { \"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 1 }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"dataMissing\",\"success\",\"minPoetics\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"version\",\"depth\",\"topN\",\"cacheSize\",\"breakerErrorThreshold\",\n    \"resetTimeout\",\"rollingWindowMs\",\"rollingBuckets\",\n    \"regression\",\"fractalOptions\",\"pythonFallback\",\"sigilAlert\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}\n```\n\n### 2.2 `validateConfig.ts`\n\nIn `packages/common/src/utils/validateConfig.ts` implementieren wir die Lade- und Validierungs­logik:\n\n```ts\nimport fs from 'fs';\nimport path from 'path';\nimport Ajv from 'ajv';\nimport schema from '../schemas/theory-agent-config.json';\n\nconst ajv = new Ajv({ allErrors: true, useDefaults: true });\nconst validate = ajv.compile<T>(schema);\n\nexport function loadConfig<T>(filePath: string): T {\n  const raw = fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf-8');\n  const ext = path.extname(filePath).toLowerCase();\n  const data = ext === '.json'\n    ? JSON.parse(raw)\n    : require('yaml').parse(raw);\n\n  if (!validate(data)) {\n    throw new Error(`Config validation failed:\n${ajv.errorsText(validate.errors)}`);\n  }\n  return data;\n}\n```\n\n### 2.3 Unit‑Tests für Config‑Validation\n\nErstelle `packages/common/src/utils/validateConfig.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { loadConfig } from './validateConfig';\nimport path from 'path';\n\ndescribe('Config Validation', () => {\n  it('should load and validate valid config', () => {\n    const cfg = loadConfig(path.resolve(__dirname, '../../config/cosmic-theory-agent.yaml'));\n    expect(cfg.depth).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    expect(cfg.regression.timeout).toBe(2000);\n  });\n\n  it('should throw on invalid config', () => {\n    expect(() => loadConfig('path/to/invalid.yaml')).toThrow();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\nNun haben wir eine robuste **Config‑Validierung** inklusive Schema, Lade-Funktion und Unit‑Tests.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Core-Layer-Framework (Composite Pattern)\n\nDieses Modul im Package `common` definiert die abstrakte Schichtstruktur für verschachtelte Layer, die in der **AeonAI-UI-Pyramid-Suite** verwendet wird.\n\n### 3.1 Interface & Basis-Implementierung\n\n```ts\n// packages/common/src/layers/Layer.ts\nexport interface EmergenceMetrics {\n  coherence: number;\n  resonance: number;\n  emergence: number;\n  poetics: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Layer {\n  id: string;\n  level: number;\n  weight: number;\n  children?: Layer[];\n  analyze(): EmergenceMetrics;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 Kosmische Gewichtungen\n\n```ts\n// packages/common/src/layers/weights.ts\nexport const PHI = (1 + Math.sqrt(5)) / 2;\nexport const PI = Math.PI;\nexport const E = Math.E;\n\n/** Gewichtung basierend auf dem goldenen Schnitt */\nexport function phiWeight(level: number): number {\n  return Math.pow(PHI, -level);\n}\n\n/** Kombinierte kosmische Gewichtung */\nexport function combinedWeight(level: number, factor: number): number {\n  return phiWeight(level) * Math.sin(PI * factor) + Math.log1p(E * factor);\n}\n```\n\n### 3.3 Generierung verschachtelter Layer\n\n```ts\n// packages/common/src/layers/generateNestedLayers.ts\nimport { Layer, EmergenceMetrics } from './Layer';\nimport { combinedWeight } from './weights';\n\n/**\n * Erzeugt einen verschachtelten Layer-Baum (Tiefe = depth, Unterteilungen = subdivisions)\n */\nexport function generateNestedLayers(depth: number, subdivisions: number): Layer {\n  function build(level: number): Layer[] {\n    if (level > depth) return [];\n    return Array.from({ length: subdivisions }, (_, idx) => {\n      const layer: Layer = {\n        id: `L${level}-N${idx}`,\n        level,\n        weight: combinedWeight(level, (idx + 1) / subdivisions),\n        children: build(level + 1),\n        analyze(): EmergenceMetrics {\n          const childMetrics = this.children?.map(c => c.analyze()) || [];\n          const sum = childMetrics.reduce((acc, m) => ({\n            coherence: acc.coherence + m.coherence,\n            resonance: acc.resonance + m.resonance,\n            emergence: acc.emergence + m.emergence,\n            poetics: acc.poetics + m.poetics\n          }), { coherence: 0, resonance: 0, emergence: 0, poetics: 0 });\n          return {\n            coherence: this.weight + sum.coherence,\n            resonance: this.weight + sum.resonance,\n            emergence: this.weight + sum.emergence,\n            poetics: this.weight + sum.poetics\n          };\n        }\n      };\n      return layer;\n    });\n  }\n\n  return {\n    id: 'root',\n    level: 0,\n    weight: 1,\n    children: build(1),\n    analyze(): EmergenceMetrics {\n      const metrics = this.children!.map(c => c.analyze());\n      return metrics.reduce((a, b) => ({\n        coherence: a.coherence + b.coherence,\n        resonance: a.resonance + b.resonance,\n        emergence: a.emergence + b.emergence,\n        poetics: a.poetics + b.poetics\n      }), { coherence: 0, resonance: 0, emergence: 0, poetics: 0 });\n    }\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### 3.4 Unit-Test\n\n```ts\n// packages/common/src/layers/generateNestedLayers.test.ts\nimport { generateNestedLayers } from './generateNestedLayers';\n\ndescribe('generateNestedLayers', () => {\n  it('should create a nested layer tree and compute metrics', () => {\n    const root = generateNestedLayers(2, 3);\n    const metrics = root.analyze();\n\n    expect(metrics.coherence).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    expect(metrics.resonance).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    expect(metrics.emergence).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    expect(metrics.poetics).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n\n    expect(root.children).toHaveLength(3);\n    root.children!.forEach(child => {\n      expect(child.children).toHaveLength(3);\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### 3.5 Integration in Agent\n\n```ts\n// packages/agent/src/agents/CosmicTheoryAgent.ts\nimport { generateNestedLayers } from 'common/layers/generateNestedLayers';\n\nconst rootLayer = generateNestedLayers(config.depth, config.subdivisions);\nconst nestedMetrics = rootLayer.analyze();\n// nutze nestedMetrics für initiale CREP-Gewichtung oder als KI-Input\n```\n\n## 6. UI-Skeleton & React + Three-Fiber-Integration Integration Agent ↔ UI\n\nFür die Kommunikation zwischen `CosmicTheoryAgent` und UI stellen wir einen einfachen HTTP-API-Server bereit.\n\n### 6.1 Agent-Server Endpoint\n\n```ts\n// packages/agent/src/server.ts\nimport express from 'express';\nimport { CosmicTheoryAgent } from './agents/CosmicTheoryAgent';\nimport bodyParser from 'body-parser';\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use(bodyParser.json());\nconst agent = new CosmicTheoryAgent(...);\n\napp.post('/api/generate', async (req, res) => {\n  const { depth, subdivisions } = req.body;\n  const formulas = await agent.generateTheories({userSessionId: req.body.sessionId});\n  res.json({ formulas });\n});\n\napp.get('/api/sigils', (req, res) => {\n  // Beispiel-Daten oder real aus config\n  res.json([{ id: 'aeon:2025-0711-EINSTEIN' }]);\n});\n\napp.get('/api/metrics', (req, res) => {\n  res.json({ coherence: 1.23, resonance: 0.98 });\n});\n\napp.listen(3000, () => console.log('Agent server listening on 3000'));\n```\n\n### 6.2 Frontend-Hook `useGenerateTheories`\n\n```ts\n// packages/ui/src/hooks/useGenerateTheories.ts\nimport { useState } from 'react';\n\nexport function useGenerateTheories() {\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);\n  const [result, setResult] = useState<any[]>([]);\n\n  async function generate(params: { depth: number; subdivisions: number }) {\n    setLoading(true);\n    const res = await fetch('/api/generate', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},\n      body: JSON.stringify(params)\n    });\n    const data = await res.json();\n    setResult(data.formulas);\n    setLoading(false);\n  }\n\n  return { generate, result, loading };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\nDamit hast du die **AudioEngine** vertieft und eine **Agent-API** samt Hook zur Integration bereitgestellt.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Observability & Telemetrie\n\nUm Traces, Logs und CREP-Metriken im UI sichtbar zu machen, fügen wir:\n\n### 7.1 OpenTelemetry im Agent\n\n```ts\n// packages/agent/src/observability/tracing.ts\nimport { NodeTracerProvider } from '@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node';\nimport { registerInstrumentations } from '@opentelemetry/instrumentation';\nimport { JaegerExporter } from '@opentelemetry/exporter-jaeger';\n\nconst provider = new NodeTracerProvider();\nprovider.addSpanProcessor(\n  new SimpleSpanProcessor(new JaegerExporter({ serviceName: 'cosmic-theory-agent' }))\n);\nprovider.register();\nregisterInstrumentations({ tracerProvider: provider, instrumentations: [] });\n```\n\n### 7.2 Metrics-Endpoint im Agent\n\n```ts\n// packages/agent/src/server.ts (Ergänzung)\nimport { collectDefaultMetrics, Registry } from 'prom-client';\nconst registry = new Registry();\ncollectDefaultMetrics({ register: registry });\n\napp.get('/metrics', async (_req, res) => {\n  res.set('Content-Type', registry.contentType);\n  res.end(await registry.metrics());\n});\n```\n\n### 7.3 Telemetry-Dashboard im UI\n\n```tsx\n// packages/ui/src/components/TelemetryDashboard.tsx\nimport React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\nimport { LineChart, Line, XAxis, YAxis, Tooltip } from 'recharts';\n\nexport function TelemetryDashboard() {\n  const [data, setData] = useState<any[]>([]);\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const interval = setInterval(async () => {\n      const resp = await fetch('/metrics');\n      const text = await resp.text();\n      // parse Prometheus metrics into chart data\n      const parsed = text.split('\n').filter(l => l.startsWith('theory_generation_duration')).map(line => {\n        const [metric, value] = line.split(' ');\n        return { metric, value: Number(value) };\n      });\n      setData(parsed);\n    }, 5000);\n    return () => clearInterval(interval);\n  }, []);\n  return (\n    <LineChart width={300} height={200} data={data}>\n      <XAxis dataKey=\"metric\" />\n      <YAxis />\n      <Tooltip />\n      <Line type=\"monotone\" dataKey=\"value\" />\n    </LineChart>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## 8. Testing & Deployment\n\n### 8.1 End-to-End Tests mit Cypress\n\n```js\n// packages/ui/cypress/integration/sigil_flow.spec.js\ndescribe('Sigil Flow', () => {\n  it('selects a sigil and triggers an alert', () => {\n    cy.visit('/');\n    cy.intercept('GET', '/api/sigils', [{id:'aeon:test'}]);\n    cy.get('select#sigil').select('aeon:test');\n    cy.get('.alert').should('contain', 'aeon:test');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### 8.2 Docker & Kubernetes\n\n**Dockerfile (UI)**\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:18-alpine AS build\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY . .\nRUN pnpm install && pnpm build\n\nFROM nginx:alpine\nCOPY --from=build /app/packages/ui/dist /usr/share/nginx/html\n```\n\n**k8s-deployment.yaml**\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: aeon-ui\nspec:\n  replicas: 2\n  selector: { matchLabels: { app: aeon-ui } }\n  template:\n    metadata: { labels: { app: aeon-ui } }\n    spec:\n      containers:\n        - name: ui\n          image: myregistry/aeon-ui:latest\n          ports: [{ containerPort: 80 }]\n```\n\n---\n\nDamit ist das **Observability-Setup**, End-to-End-Testing und die **Deployment-Pipeline** in Docker & Kubernetes komplett umgesetzt. Viel Erfolg beim Ausrollen deines AeonAI-UI-Pyramid-Universums! 🚀                     Ich habe Abschnitt 3 komplett neu strukturiert und korrigiert:\n\n    Einheitliche Nummerierung von 3.1 bis 3.5\n\n    Entfernung doppelter bzw. fehlerhafter Snippets\n\n    Konsistente Code-Fences und präzise Beschreibungen\n\nAlle nachfolgenden Sections (ab ## 6) bleiben erhalten."
